description:
Direct contradiction between documented contract and implemented behavior.

The CtLog field doc (pkix-ct/src/log_list.rs:46):
\`\`\`
/// First moment the log is considered usable, in milliseconds
/// since the Unix epoch. SCTs with timestamps before this point
/// are not trustworthy even if signed by this log's key. \`None\`
/// means the log has never reached the \`usable\` state.
\`\`\`

The implementation (pkix-ct/src/verify.rs:845-857):
\`\`\`
fn log_window_contains(log: &CtLog, timestamp_ms: u64) -> bool {
    if let Some(lo) = log.usable_from_ms {
        if timestamp_ms < lo {
            return false;
        }
    }
    // ... if None, fall through and treat all timestamps as in-window
\`\`\`

If a log has \`usable_from_ms = None\` (\"never reached usable state\"), then by the docstring NO SCT from that log should be trusted. But \`log_window_contains\` returns \`true\` for any timestamp, so \`verify_sct_for_cert\` / \`verify_sct_for_precert\` will accept SCTs from never-usable logs.

This is the same class of issue PKIX-q74z.10 flagged for the Google JSON parser (silent acceptance of pending/qualified/rejected logs), but with the bug surfaced one layer deeper: the field-semantics doc contradicts the validation primitive.

Caller-impact: a caller who manually constructs a \`CtLog\` with \`usable_from_ms = None\` (per the doc, intending \"do not trust\") will find that pkix-ct trusts SCTs from that log anyway. This is a verifier-soundness gap, not just a documentation paper-cut.

Fix shape, one of:
1. \`log_window_contains\` returns \`false\` when \`usable_from_ms == None\` (matches docstring intent).
2. Change the CtLog docstring to say \`None\` means \"unbounded — log is usable for all timestamps\" (matches code). This is dangerous because it silently widens trust.
3. Use a more explicit type — \`enum LogWindow { Bounded { from_ms, until_ms: Option<u64> }, NeverUsable }\` — and force the construction to be unambiguous.

Recommend (1): per the docstring, the soundness-preserving choice is to reject when \`None\`.

Relates to PKIX-q74z.10 (parser-side cousin) and PKIX-q74z.16 (window-bounds semantics).
